note.text:
If two figures are similar with linear scale factor k:
• lengths are multiplied by k;
• areas are multiplied by k²;
• volumes (and masses of the same material) are multiplied by k³.
Going back: if areas are in the ratio 4 : 9, lengths are in the ratio 2 : 3 (square roots); if volumes are in the ratio 8 : 27, lengths are 2 : 3 (cube roots).
